    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Johnson returns six months after his first visit and four weeks after his back strain, which settled within a week. His mood is good: he has finished a large part of his book and is back among his friends every day. Night sweats are less. He finished the eight sessions of behavioral therapy for tics in the summer and still uses the competing responses when he wants to; he says the remaining tics bother other people more than they bother him. His fecal immunochemical test and HIV test from the preventive visit were negative. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>100 mg daily</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 4; GAD-7 5</td></tr><tr><td>Tics</td><td>Behavioral therapy completed</td></tr><tr><td>Back</td><td>Resolved</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

